The graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,-1) -- (1,3);
\draw[fill=white] (1,3) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick, ->] (1,-1) -- (4,-1);
\fill (1,-1) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the value of $f(1)$?

The graph of $y = g(x)$ is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-4.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.5) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-4,4) -- (-2,4);
\fill (-2,4) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick, ->] (-2,1) -- (2,5);
\draw[fill=white] (-2,1) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the value of $g(-2)$?
